+## Beginner display update — 26 September 2026
+
+The home view presents one model at a time, starting with twist geometry. The model selector and previous/next buttons retain access to all six exhibits. Explanations and methods remain available beneath each exhibit.
+
+The moiré view defaults to a fitted, full-cell illustration. Its normalized three-harmonic alignment guide is `(cos(u)+cos(v)+cos(u+v)+1.5)/4.5`, where `u=2π(x/√3+y)/L` and `v=-4πx/(√3L)`. Contrast mapping is for legibility; it is not a calculated energy, density, or quantitative registry observable. Both primitive cell translations preserve this illustration. The layers view retains the actual symmetrically rotated triangular reference sites with cyan filled dots and orange rings. It opens at 3 nm; fit-cell and zoom buttons change the physical viewing window, preserving equal x/y scales. No scientific data or audit verdict changed.
+
+Validation: DOM interactions, model selection, display modes, zoom and cell labels at 0.50°, 0.58°, 1.05° and 3.00° passed, together with existing coverage-data checks. Managed visual preview remains blocked by the absent `/tmp/sites-previewd/requests` mailbox; browser/GPU visual verification is pending.
